<title>LITHUANIA: PRESIDENT NAMES HEAD OF SECURITIES COMMISSION.</title>
<headline>PRESIDENT NAMES HEAD OF SECURITIES COMMISSION.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lithuanian President Algirdas Brazauskas issued a decree on Monday appointing Virgilijus Poderys as head of the country's securities commission, the president's office said.</p>
<p>The president's office said in a statement that the decree will come into effect after the Lithuanian parliament accepts the resignation of Algirdas Shemeta from the post, who left to become minister of finance.</p>
<p>The statement said that Poderys' term of office would last until June 18, 2001.</p>
<p>Poderys, 36, is currently the deputy chairman of the securities commission.</p>
<p>--Andrius Vilkancas, Vilnius newsroom +370 2 22 35 17</p>
